<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n105842" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τυκτός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεύχω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>finished, wrought out,</i> i. e.
				<i>complete,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τυκτὸν κακόν,</span> of Ares, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				5.831
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρήνη τυκτή</span> a fountain
				<i>made by man's hand,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				17.206
			</span></i>: then, <i>well-made, well-wrought,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τυκτῇσι βόεσσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					12.105
				</span></i>
			; of a bowling-green, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν τ. δαπέδῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					4.627
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				17.169
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τυκτὴ μάρμαρος,</span> of a
			tombstone, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				22.210
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
